; S12: a `:lowering :produces` head may name a slot-local form. The
; `test/nest-emit-v1` hook lowers `(seed)` into `(wrap (leaf))`, and `leaf`
; is declared *inside* `wrap` — a positional slot-local, the S7 shape whose
; whole point is that no global `leaf` exists. The contract walk checks every
; emitted head at every depth, so `leaf` must be in `:produces`; and it now
; resolves there: a bare head resolves local-first, to a slot-local form
; reachable through a form the same list resolves (`wrap`). Before, this
; manifest was stuck between `lowering_produced_invalid_head` (`leaf`
; absent from the list) and `unknown_form` at schema load (`leaf` present).
(plugin :name p :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name seed :open true
    :lowering (lowering :hook test/nest-emit-v1 :produces [wrap leaf]))
  (form :name wrap
    (form :name leaf)))

(seed)
